From: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
Subject: [PATCH] mmc: ingenic: use host->pdata in present_store

ingenic_mmc_present_store() reads dev->platform_data, which is NULL for a
device-tree probed host. Writing INSERT/REMOVE to the sysfs "present" node
then faults on pdata->removal. Every other use of pdata in the driver takes
it from host->pdata; do the same here so the non-removable path (used by the
T31 SDIO WLAN init to force a rescan after power-on) works.

Signed-off-by: Paul Philippov <paul@themactep.com>
---
 drivers/mmc/host/ingenic_mmc.c | 3 +--
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/drivers/mmc/host/ingenic_mmc.c
+++ b/drivers/mmc/host/ingenic_mmc.c
@@ -1302,2 +1302,2 @@
-	struct ingenic_mmc_pdata *pdata = dev->platform_data;
 	struct ingenic_mmc_host *host = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
+	struct ingenic_mmc_pdata *pdata = host->pdata;
